{"id":"word:hebrew:H8432","type":"word","title":"תָּוֶךְ","subtitle":"H8432 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a bisection , i.e. (by implication) the centre","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to תָּוֶךְ (H8432) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 420 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"תָּוֶךְ (tâvek) means a bisection , i.e. (by implication) the centre First listed occurrence: 1Chr 11 14."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"תָּוֶךְ","transliteration":"tâvek","pronunciation":"taw'-vek","strong":"H8432","lemmaId":"hebrew:H8432","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["בְּ/ת֣וֹךְ","בְּ/ת֥וֹךְ","בְּ/ת֖וֹךְ","מִ/תּ֣וֹךְ","תּ֣וֹךְ"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncmsc",240],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3mp",44],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3fs",36],["HNcmsc",25],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp2mp",17],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp2fs",16],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",10],["HC/R/Ncmsc",8],["HRd/Ncmsa",5],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp1cp",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"a bisection , i.e. (by implication) the centre","usage":"among(-st), × between, half, × (there-, where-), in(-to), middle, mid(-night), midst (among), × out (of), × through, × with(-in).","full":"H8432. tavek תָּ֫וֶךְ 418 substantive midst (Late Hebrew id. , also denominative תִּוֵּוךְ ; √ unknown; not apparently in cognate languages); — absolute תָּ֫וֶךְ Gen 15:10 +; construct תּוֺךְ 1:6 +; תּוֺכוֺ תּוֺכִי, , etc., 2 feminine singular כִי תּוֺכֵּ֫ Psa 116:19 ; 135:9 , תּוֺכֹה Ezek 48:15 , 21 , תּוֺכֲכֶם Gen 23:9 +, תּוֺכָ֫הְנָה Ezek 16:53 (Ges § 91f ); — midst , whether of a space or place, a number of people or things, or of a linE: absolute Judg 16:29 הַתָּוֶךְ עַמּוּדֵי = the middle columns, Jer 39:3 בַּתָּוֶךְ הַתּ, ׳שַׁעַר Gen 15:10 בַּתּ ׳אֹתָם וַיְבַתֵּר , Num 35:5 בַּתָּוֶךְ וְהָעִיר , Josh 8:22 ; Judg 15:4 ; Isa 66:17 בַּתָּוֶךְ אֶחָד אַחַר ; construct 1Kin 8:54 הֶחָצֵר תּוֺךְ אֶתֿ הַמֶּלֶךְ קִדַּשׁ , Ezek 15:4 נָחָר וְתוֺכוֺ ; usually with preposition, as בְּ (often = an emphasis in , in the very heart and midst of), Gen 1:6 הַמַּיִם בְּתוֺךְ , 2:9 ׳בְּת הַגָּן , 9:21 ׳בְּת אָהֳהֹ , 18:24 ׳בְּת הָעִיר , 37:7 ׳בְּת הַשָּׁדֶה , Exod 11:4 ׳בת מצרים יוצא אני , 39:3 , Josh 8:9 ׳בְּת הָעָם , Judg 7:16 ׳בת דִּים הַכַּ , 1Kin 3:20 ׳בְּת הַלַּיְלָה ; בְּתוֺכָהּ (of land or city) Num 13:32 ; Isa 7:6 , etc.; in Ezekiel בְּתוֺכָהּ בְּתוֺכֵךְ, , etc., of sins done, or judgment to be wrought, in the very midst of Jerusalem, Ezek 5:8 , 10 ; 9:4 ; 22:3 , 7 , 9 , 13 +; ׳בְּת מֵעַי Psa 22:15 ; 40:9 ׳בְּת לִבִּי בְּת, ׳תּוֺרָֽתְךָ מֵעָ֫י 22:11 , compare Prov 4:21 ; after verbs of motion, = into Exod 14:27 ; 1Sam 9:14 , = through Exod 14:29 ; Num 33:8 ; Ezek 9:4 ; Neh 9:11 ; of a number of persons = among (not nEcess. of the actual middle ), Gen 40:20 בְּתוֺכְנוּ ׳בְּת, עֲבָדָיו 23:6 , בְּתוֺכָם 1Sam 10:10 ; Job 1:6 , etc., בְּתוֺכֲכֶם הַגָּר Lev 17:8 , 10 , 13 +; = between (of things arranged by twos) Exod 39:25 in P often (12 t.) of the divinE presence, or dwelling, in the midst of Israel, 25:8 ; 29:45-46 , Lev 15:31 ; 16:16 + (Carpenter Hex. i. 209, ed. 2, 410 ; J E D in such cases have always קֶרֶב ), so Ezek 37:26 , 28 ; 43:7 , 9 , compare Hag 2:5 ; מִן , as Gen 19:29 הַהֲפֵכָה מִתּוֺךְ , Exod 3:2 הַסְּנֶה ׳מִתּ , 33:11 מִתּ יָמִישׁ ׳לאֹ הָאֹהֶל , Deut 4:12 + ׳מִתּ הָאֵשׁ , 1Sam 15:6 מִתּ ׳רְדוּ עֲמָלֵק ; = from among , as to take, separate, etc., ׳מִתּ הָעָם מִתּוֺכָם, , etc., Exod 7:5 ; 28:1 ; Num 3:12 ; 4:2 , 18 ; 16:21 , 33 ; 17:10 ; 19:20 (all P) +; אֶל , as Exod 14:23 הַיָּם ויבאואֶ֗֗֗לאתּוֺךְ , Lev 11:33 ; Num 17:12 ׳אֶלאתּ הַקָּהָל וַיָּרָץ , 19:6 ; Deut 21:12 אֶלאתּ ׳וַהֲבֵאתָהּ בֵּיתֶ֫ךָ , 22:2 ; 23:11 ; 2Sam 3:27 ; 4:6 ; Jer 21:4 +; מֵעַל Ezek 11:23 . &#8212; תוך is used by most writers, occurring approximately 8-10 times in many books, but is especially frequent in P (c. 106 t,) and Ezekiel (116 t.). synonym קֶרֶב , q. v.","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to sever ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary